<Layout title='My Skills'>
    <h2>hello world</h2>
    <p>People have always wanted to improve their lives. “Engineer” is a job title that specializes in solving problems, and its main goal is to improve people’s lives. Although engineers help improve quality of life, life is big. We need many types of engineers to focus on specific areas. An example is Bioengineering, a type of engineering that directly solves problems related to quality of life.</p>
    <p>First of all, Bioengineering is a huge field. There are many aspects of nature to consider, which is why bioengineering has subfields. Each subfield will focus on a specific area. For example, bioengineers work in many areas like medicine, agriculture, and the environment. In medicine, bioengineers will create products that will be helpful for patients or support hospitals. Some of their products that have been developed and used are X-ray scanners, heart rate monitors, and hearing aids. People’s lives have been so much better after those products were invented. In agriculture, bioengineers take care of plants or crops. They modify the genes in the plants to make them be able to survive in harsh environments. They have another subfield named “Genetic Engineering” for this type of work. In the environment, bioengineers are trying to solve problems that people have created a long time ago. It is pollution. Air and plastic are two major problems that we are currently facing. Bioengineers are trying to speed up the process of things breaking down. It will reduce the amount of plastic on the Earth. What they do is just to convert plastic into other materials. They can’t just destroy plastic based on the law of conservation of mass; mass can’t be created or destroyed. For air pollution, they also use a similar solution. The Biomitech company has BioUrban, an artificial tree that uses microalgae to clean the urban air. This building basically turns gases like CO2 or NO2 into O2. All of those examples show us that bioengineering will help us improve our lives.</p>
    <p>However, people are still worried about prices or safety. Although we have those smart inventions, bioengineering is still facing some questions about ethical issues or safety. In my opinion, technology always faces those questions, and they still find other ways to achieve their goal without conflicts with any of those questions.</p>
    <p>We can make our Earth greener and fresher. Besides the environment, bioengineers also take cares about medical field. It’s just about time for this potential field to give us a more convenience live.</p>
</Layout>